/*! \page sdk_reference_packages Reference Package Inventory

Markdown companion: \c docs/reference_packages.md.
Enable/run every package: \c docs/run_examples.md.

\section sdk_ref_a Class A

CPU and CUDA modules for CE (\c 0x00010003), CE+EQ (\c 0x00010004), and
receiver (\c 0x00010005): \c ref_channel_estimator_*, \c ref_equalizer_*,
\c ref_receiver_*. CUDA variants require resident device tensors and inherit
\c invocation.execution_stream.

SRS channel estimator (\c 0x00010007): \c ref_srs_channel_estimator_cpu and
\c ref_srs_channel_estimator_cuda reproduce the gNB's host SRS estimator and are
checked against OCUDU-generated golden vectors (\c tests/data); the reader is
\c ocudu_dapp_sdk/srs_channel_estimator_vectors.h and \c ocudu-dapp-srs-replay
replays vector files, including live captures from \c examples/e3_srs_dataset.

\section sdk_ref_b Class B

\c ref_scheduler_cpu only. Baseline-replica host-record pipeline (rank / OLLA /
MCS / multi-UE pack / TPC) plus optional PRB avoid mask; emits only host-allowed
intents. See \ref sdk_class_b and \c docs/class_b_scheduler_baseline.md.

\section sdk_ref_c Class C

Native CPU/CUDA spectrum and SRS--ISAC; process workers
\c ref_spectrumd_*, \c ref_srs_isacd_*, \c ref_spectrum_observerd_cpu; CUDA-IPC
workers \c ref_spectrumd_cuda and \c ref_srs_isacd_cuda. Portable E3 consumers
\c ref_spectrum_e3_cpu and \c ref_srs_isac_e3_cpu are independent binaries, not
catalog packages.

Python research examples (\c examples/class_c_e3_python): catalog packages
\c class_c_python_spectrumd / \c class_c_python_srs_isacd and optional portable
E3. Python is Class-C out-of-process only and not a production performance path.

\section sdk_ref_test Test-only

Joint multi-interface, multi-input fusion, failure gallery, and certifier-bad
modules exist only when \c BUILD_TESTING is enabled. Do not deploy them to
production catalogs.

*/
